What does a Senior Creative Technologist do at WPP Production?

The Senior Creative Technologist oversees the definition, architecture, and execution of generative AI workflows&nbsp; used to create high-quality creative marketing content . Positioned at the intersection of creative craft, marketing, generative AI, and production systems, this role is responsible for translating marketing briefs and creative requirements into repeatable generation approaches across copy, imagery, video, templates, and other content format.&nbsp; &nbsp;

In addition to hands-on prototyping and technical pipeline design, the Senior Creative Technologist will lead and oversee the work of other creative technologists. You will guide team members in defining technical requirements, establishing deliverable specifications, and ensuring final output meet s delivery benchmarks. Through active mentorship, coaching, and technical guidance, you will empower the team to deliver high-quality work. &nbsp;

Beyond imparting technical skills, this role is about shaping well-rounded creative technologists who are equipped with the soft skills needed to thrive in advertising : presenting, collaboration, client relations, self-confidence, and professional communication. &nbsp;

The Senior Creative Technologist will also serve as technical lead for special projects across a wide variety of formats which may include physical-digital installations, creative computing applications, AR/VR spatial experiences, mobile and desktop gaming applications, and real-time 3D environments. &nbsp;

This role requires someone with proven experience in the creative technology field who is constantly pushing their own craft and re-educating themselves on the latest tools and pipelines. They should be deeply familiar with collaborative work, managing multi-disciplinary projects, and delivering client work; because they'll be preparing others to do the same. They will need to be able to understand and identify automation use cases for and with clients.  &nbsp;

